  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 227 AM CDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nHigh pressure continues to bring hot and dry conditions to our area. \nWhile Saharan dust and smoke from agricultural fires will create \nhazy skies next week, it's still too early to tell if this haze will \noffer any real relief from the heat. For now, the forecast remains \nunchanged.\n\nExpect heat index values between 100 and 109 through the weekend and \ninto early next week. If you are spending time outdoors, please stay \nsafe: take frequent breaks, stay hydrated with water, and don't \nforget your sunscreen. More heat safety information can be found at \nweather.gov/heat",
